From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:01:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] AROS: hx-editor refuses to start without the hx
 launcher

The LSP build runs the editor on the program's own task (vfork from a
pthread fails on AROS One), which needs a 16 MiB stack. Started directly
from a Shell with its default stack, it would overflow. The hx launcher
sets HELIX_PROGDIR; without it hx-editor says to use hx and ends with 20.
---
 helix-term/src/main.rs | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/helix-term/src/main.rs b/helix-term/src/main.rs
index 0778ec96d9904d028e43aca90b5ba2f6d91ee943..55041a88d46086299d697a909df85cc6110a1002 100644
--- a/helix-term/src/main.rs
+++ b/helix-term/src/main.rs
@@ -44,6 +44,12 @@ fn main() -> Result<()> {
 // futures on the initialized main task; this does not qualify cancellation.
 #[cfg(target_os = "aros")]
 fn main() -> Result<()> {
+    // The hx launcher runs this program with the 16 MiB stack it needs and
+    // sets HELIX_PROGDIR; started directly, it would overflow a Shell's stack.
+    if std::env::var_os("HELIX_PROGDIR").is_none() {
+        eprintln!("hx-editor: start Helix with the hx program next to it (it sets the stack Helix needs).");
+        std::process::exit(20);
+    }
     std::process::exit(main_impl()?);
 }
 
